Z||000019||artherd||11-13-2001||05:48 AM||||Nice, looks like we share a similar taste in the Ulitmate Driving machine ;) Heh, it's an ongoing search, I'm actually hoping to find one with something easially fixable to knock the price down a bit :) (like a siezed differential or such, something I can replace fairly easially and inexpensively.)<P>They run in the $15-20k range in the US for one with ~80kmiles (not so cheap for a CSI, but the earlier 6-speed ci and i models)<BR>Yeah, I don't get it either, I mean, they're *fabaolus* cars, $80-100K new not just a few years ago!<BR>A true exotic for a honda price?!  Oh yeah!!<BR>Michilin I belive uses a modified 850 to test   and develop their performance tyres... (nothing like a 350+ (easially a big 'plus')hp hugely fast car that also weighs almost 5,000lbs :)<BR>It'll probally take me a while to find the right car (I want a Calipso Red / light creame interior 850CSI, but I'll settle for a decent mechanically good 6-speed 850 of any sort ;)  <P>Hrm... wondering how much it'd be to ship a car from Germany...<P>Heh, I looked actively for my ttop car for well over 2 years, waiting sucks, but the cars you end up with are worth it! ;)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clube31.multimania.com/Members/files/Back_View_of_BMW__V12.jpg"> <BR>Only car I've ever seen make 18" wheels look small :)<BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
