Z||000021||Formula88||11-13-2001||09:06 AM||||Nice choice on cars, Ben.  When I found out how cheap 850's were, I started thinking.  Probably a dangerous thing to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'd love to get just about any 850 - even an automatic.  Since it fits the style of luxo cruiser as well as autobahn stormer, the auto isn't out of character.  Still, the 6-speed would be preferable.  I always loved them when they came out - but just a dream machine.  Now, I might be able to afford a second hand dream for the price of a late model used Trans Am.  Um, ok!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh, my "beater" is a '99 Grand Am SE1.  3400SFI V6 - and red, of course.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||Screwie||11-13-2001||10:55 AM||||I got one of the brochures of the 850 they printed a couple of years ago when they first came out. It's huge and they normally just lent it to potential customers, cause it was really expensive. They gave me one cause I am such a huge BMW freak!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> In that brochure, the main 850 they show is exactly the one you want  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I wish I could scan it in for you, but it's really huge, it's A3 size  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The main problem with owning one in Holland is you have to pay taxes according to the cars weight... Wellp, you can imagine how much that would cost me, so even though it's kind of affordable here, with insurance, taxes and gas (which is 5 times more expensive here, so a V12...hmmm... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) I don't even want to calculate how much that would cost me.||||reg||1
